;
; How Bowline files a task in MYRA: its number, its list, the day its
; repeats count from and the day it is due (days since 1970: seven digits
; reach 9999-12-31), how many days or weeks apart it repeats (0: once),
; its unit (1 days, 7 weeks), the weekdays it skips as a mask (bit 0
; Monday .. bit 6 Sunday) and whether it is done (1) or open (0). The
; rules say what the values may mean (bowline_rules.h BW3); this says
; whether they make a record.
^ZXTASK(task:i9) = list:i3! ^ start:i7! ^ due:i7! ^ every:i4! ^ unit:i1! ^ skip:i3! ^ done:i1!
